  },
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math> be the length of three sides of a triangle satisfying the condition <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. If the set of all possible values of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "36",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></math></p><p>Now, we know that the sum of two sides is always greater than the third side of a triangle,</p><p>Now, taking <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Similarly, for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mo>∞</mo><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>∪</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>∞</mo></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>And for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>So, from the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo> </mo><mo>&amp;</mo><mo> </mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><msqrt><mn>5</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p>"
  }
}